.TH "ROARK\-PHONE\-NUMBER\-AVAILABLE\-LIST" "1" "" "roark-phone-number-available-list" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-phone\-number\-available\-list \- Search available phone numbers
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark phone\-number available list
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Returns US or Canadian numbers the carrier has for sale, local or toll\-free, narrowed by area code or by digits the number must contain. When an area code has no numbers, nearby ones are returned flagged bestEffort; an empty list means nothing matched. Buy one with POST /v1/phone\-number, or let Roark pick with autoPick.
.SH "API"
GET /v1/phone\-number/available
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-country\fR \fI<value>\fR
ISO 3166\-1 alpha\-2 country of the number: US or CA One of: US, CA. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-number\-type\fR \fI<value>\fR
LOCAL for a number in an area code, TOLL_FREE for one from the shared US and Canada toll\-free pool One of: LOCAL, TOLL_FREE. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-area\-code\fR \fI<value>\fR
Three\-digit area code, or a toll\-free prefix such as 800. When it has no numbers, nearby ones are returned instead, flagged bestEffort. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-contains\fR \fI<value>\fR
Digits or letters the number must contain (1 to 7, * matches any digit) Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<value>\fR
Maximum number of results (default: 20, max: 100) Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
